  "assumes": [
    {
      "note": "Every await is an interleaving point at which any other modelled action may run. This over-approximates JavaScript scheduling (a user stop arrives as a macrotask and can only land between microtasks when it is itself issued from a microtask chain), so the model may show interleavings the event loop makes rare, never fewer."
    },
    {
      "note": "The runner promise (runAgent/resumeAgent) settles exactly once, with any of: success or a non-limit failure, a usage-limit failure, or a rejection (on the spawn path also an aborted run). Whether an aborted run settles promptly is not modelled.",
      "file": ".pi/packages/choco-pi-subagents/src/agent-runner.ts"
    },
    {
      "note": "The owner's usage-limit policy is installed for the whole run; its preference/corroboration answers are free choices. The policy-missing branches of wakeUsageLimited and the poll-deadline arithmetic of armUsageWake are abstracted to a nondeterministic give-up.",
      "file": ".pi/packages/choco-pi-subagents/src/usage-limit-seam.ts"
    },
    {
      "note": "git worktree cleanup always completes, so every finishDeferredWorktreeThen callback eventually runs; its duration is unbounded."
    },
    {
      "note": "The /stop latch is always open: requireAdmissionOpen, isAdmissionOpen and refuseClosedStart are not modelled (the stop-control model is a separate target).",
      "file": ".pi/extensions/lib/stop-control.ts"
    },
    {
      "note": "Not modelled: suspend/dispose/revival/journal, run budgets (forcedStatus), parent abort signals, nested children (abortOwnedChildren, depth), workflow and /btw records (canParkForReset is always true), steering, drainQueue's provider-block/repark/start-throws branches, and cancelUsageLimitWaits."
    },
    {
      "note": "onComplete may throw (EnvCallbackMayThrow = TRUE); every call site contains it in the current code."
    },
    {
      "note": "Resumes and result reads may happen at any point, including while a stopped post-reset continuation's worktree cleanup is pending (the earlier EnvActDuringDroppedCleanup = FALSE exclusion was removed with the dropped-wake fix). Only the stopRecord path of that fix is modelled; cancelUsageLimitWaits, refuseClosedStart, drainQueue's start-throws branch and startRevivedContinuation's start failure follow the same rule and are covered by package tests."
    },
    {
      "note": "recordRunVerdict is modelled only as the await it puts on a settle path, and only for runs in VerdictRole (recordsVerdict: a verdict task and a verdict role); other runs settle without it. Its record fields and result-line append are not modelled.",
      "file": ".pi/packages/choco-pi-subagents/src/agent-manager.ts"
    },
    {
      "note": "Bounds: two agents, one pool slot, generation 3 (2 for resume-ignores-publication). Agent a1 exercises every caller action, spawns with a worktree and is a verdict-role run; a2 only spawns and resumes in the background, has no verdict await, and is never read. VerdictRole = {}, {a2} and {a1, a2} were checked once and pass."
    },
    {
      "note": "resume and revive first await a usage-limit closure re-check when a closure blocks; nothing is read or changed before that await, so it is the same Resume taking place later. Provider closures, their re-check, and startAgent's reopen after a successful run are not modelled.",
      "file": ".pi/packages/choco-pi-subagents/src/agent-manager.ts"
    }
  ],
  "checkedAt": {
    "commit": "4de824bc8928a27bbb3585ccd8f6af9c883a31d6"
  }
